   <indicator measure="2">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 2  Indicator 2</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output: Main canal water supply systems modernized 
Indicator: Improved water allocation for at least 8% of serviced farms managed by women 
Achievement: 0 
Progress/Status: Construction works are still ongoing. Project implementation and modernization of irrigation systems as well as commencement of SCADA system will allow improving the water allocation for famers at the project area. As a part of satisfactory assessment, the female headed farmers will be interviewed to assess the improvements of water allocation to them. 

In September 2023, a training workshop was conducted in the Jondor district of Bukhara region for women and farm workers, aimed at enhancing agricultural skills and knowledge. Additionally, on March 26, 2025, a training seminar on Social Guarantees and Gender Issues was held in Termez under the Babatag subproject. This seminar focused on raising awareness and improving understanding of gender equality, the role of women in agriculture and water management, social guarantees, and available opportunities for the agricultural development of women engaged in cluster, farmer, dehkan, and household farming, as well as in the water sector. A similar training session is planned to take place in Jondor in 2025. To further support capacity building, the Contract CAWRMP-CS-02 &#x201c;Capacity Building Consultants for Output 3 was signed in 2024 which includes the design and implementation of targeted training programs. Development of these training programs is currently underway.
 
Data Source: PIU quarterly progress reports, MWR reports, and BISAs&amp;apos; annual monitoring reports and water accounts</narrative>
    </description>
